# Practical 05 - Event Binding

## Aim

To demonstrate Event Binding in Angular.

## Theory

Event Binding is used to perform an action when an event occurs.

1.app.component.ts
import { Component } from '@angular/core';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-root',
  templateUrl: './app.component.html',
  styleUrls: ['./app.component.css']
})
export class AppComponent {

  message = '';

  showMessage() {
    this.message = 'Hello! Button clicked successfully.';
  }

}

2. app.component.html
<div class="container">

  <h1>Event Binding Example</h1>

  <button (click)="showMessage()">
    Click Me
  </button>

  <p>{{ message }}</p>

</div>

